<BaseLayout
  title="Atriveo Privacy | Brand Website and Public Data Notice"
  description="Read how the Atriveo brand website handles analytics, public GitHub metadata, infrastructure request logs, external product links, and personal information."
>
  <article class="legal-page section-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal / Updated October 1, 2026</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="legal-intro">Atriveo.com is a public index of Atriveo projects. Individual products may have their own privacy notices and data practices.</p>
    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <p>This brand site does not require an account and does not intentionally collect personal information through forms. Standard infrastructure logs may contain request metadata used for security and reliability.</p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>This site uses Google Analytics to understand which pages are visited and how people arrive. Google Analytics sets cookies and receives information such as pages viewed, referring site, approximate location, and device type. You can block it with a browser extension or by declining cookies in your browser.</p>
    <h2>Links to Atriveo products</h2>
    <p>When you open an Atriveo product, that product’s own privacy notice governs its handling of account and product data.</p>
    <h2>Public GitHub information</h2>
    <p>The open-source page displays metadata and activity that GitHub already makes public. Private repository names and activity are not intentionally published.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions, use the contact information published on the linked GitHub profile.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
